  "result": "`Cart.remove('sku-1')` now removes the Widget line. All 7 tests pass, and the demo prints `1`, which is just the Gadget left.\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/models.py:33`, `Cart.remove` compared the SKU you pass in against the item's *name*: `l.item.name != sku`. `'sku-1'` never equals `'Widget'`, so no line was ever removed.\n\n**Fix:** it now compares against `l.item.sku`, the same field `Cart.add` matches on.\n\nI also added a regression test, `test_remove_by_sku`, in `tests/test_orders.py`. It builds the same cart as the demo and checks that only `sku-2` remains after removing `sku-1`. Note that there's no `python` on this machine, so run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.",
